            <ArticleTitle>Rare gripping object in electrocution: Cadaveric spasm at its best.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-158</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0025817216688852</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cadaveric spasm causes instantaneous rigor without preceding post-mortem flaccidity. The precise pathophysiological basis of this phenomenon is still unknown. We report a case of accidental electrocution where the deceased was found dead with a metallic water supply pipe of a motor booster pump firmly gripped in his hand. In this report, we review the literature and consider the mechanisms that may cause this phenomenon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
